<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">1 December in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">8 events that happened on 1 December, from 800 to 1990.</p></header>
<div class="tih-pinned-card"><p class="tih-pinned-label">International day</p><p class="tih-pinned-title">World AIDS Day</p><p class="tih-pinned-desc">The first ever global health day when it launched in 1988, World AIDS Day calls on individuals, communities, and governments to unite in the fight against HIV, remember those who have died, and support the more than 38 million people living with the virus.</p></div>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/charlemagne" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/charlemagne.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/800">800 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">1,226 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Charlemagne convenes an assembly in Rome to judge Pope Leo III</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">A week after arriving in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charlemagne">Charlemagne</a> called an assembly in St Peter's to hear charges against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pope-leo-iii">Pope Leo III</a>, who cleared himself by oath. On Christmas Day Leo crowned Charlemagne emperor.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/carolingian-empire">Carolingian Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pope-leo-iii">Pope Leo III</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charlemagne">Charlemagne</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1420">1420 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">606 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Henry V enters Paris in triumph</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Henry V of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a> rode into <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paris">Paris</a> alongside <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-vi-of-france">Charles VI of France</a>. Under the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-troyes">Treaty of Troyes</a> he was regent and heir to the French throne, but his death in 1422 left the dual monarchy to his infant son.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paris">Paris</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1640">1640 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">386 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Portuguese conspirators end Spanish rule in Lisbon</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Nobles stormed the royal palace in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lisbon">Lisbon</a> and proclaimed the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/john-iv-of-portugal">Duke of Braganza</a> king as John IV. The coup ended 60 years of union with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a>; the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/house-of-braganza">Braganza dynasty</a> reigned until 1910.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lisbon">Lisbon</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1828">1828 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">198 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Juan Lavalle overthrows Governor Manuel Dorrego in Buenos Aires</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Returning with troops who had fought in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cisplatine-war">Cisplatine War</a>, Juan Lavalle of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/unitarian-party">Unitarian Party</a> mounted a coup in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/buenos-aires">Buenos Aires</a> Province, deposing Governor Manuel Dorrego, whom he captured and killed. The coup reignited the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/argentine-civil-wars">Argentine Civil Wars</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/argentine-civil-wars">Argentine Civil Wars</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1913">1913 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">113 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Ford installs a moving assembly line for the whole car</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">At Highland Park, Michigan, Ford began building the Model T on a moving assembly line. Assembly time fell from over 12 hours to about 90 minutes, and cheap cars reshaped modern industry.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1955">1955 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">71 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Rosa Parks refuses to give up her bus seat</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rosa-parks">Rosa Parks</a> was arrested in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/montgomery-alabama">Montgomery, Alabama</a>, for refusing to give her seat to a white passenger. The 381-day bus boycott that followed brought <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/martin-luther-king-jr">Martin Luther King Jr.</a> to national prominence.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1959">1959 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">67 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Twelve nations sign the Antarctic Treaty</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">In Washington, twelve countries, including the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/soviet-union">Soviet Union</a>, agreed to reserve Antarctica for peaceful scientific research. The treaty banned military activity and froze territorial claims.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/soviet-union">Soviet Union</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1990">1990 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">36 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Tunnellers from Britain and France meet under the Channel</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">British and French workers broke through the last wall of rock and shook hands beneath the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/english-channel">English Channel</a>. The tunnel opened in 1994, linking <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a> to the Continent by rail.</p></div></li></ol>
<section class="day-ppl" aria-labelledby="day-born"><h2 class="ref-sec-title" id="day-born">Born on 1 December <span class="n">6</span></h2><ul class="enc-seealso"><li><a href="/encyclopedia/louis-vi-of-france"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/louis-vi-of-france.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Louis VI of France</span><span class="tp">1081–1137</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/peter-ii-duke-of-bourbon"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/peter-ii-duke-of-bourbon.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Peter II, Duke of Bourbon</span><span class="tp">1438–1503</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/takeda-shingen"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/takeda-shingen.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Takeda Shingen</span><span class="tp">1521–1573</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/vaira-vike-freiberga"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/vaira-vike-freiberga.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Vaira Vīķe-Freiberga</span><span class="tp">b. 1937</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/sebastian-pinera"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/sebastian-pinera.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Sebastián Piñera</span><span class="tp">1949–2024</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/pablo-escobar"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/pablo-escobar.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Pablo Escobar</span><span class="tp">1949–1993</span></span></a></li></ul></section>
<section class="day-ppl" aria-labelledby="day-died"><h2 class="ref-sec-title" id="day-died">Died on 1 December <span class="n">6</span></h2><ul class="enc-seealso"><li><a href="/encyclopedia/thietmar-of-merseburg"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/thietmar-of-merseburg.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Thietmar of Merseburg</span><span class="tp">975–1018</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/emperor-go-komatsu"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/emperor-go-komatsu.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Emperor Go-Komatsu</span><span class="tp">1377–1433</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/margaret-of-austria-duchess-of-savoy"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/margaret-of-austria-duchess-of-savoy.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Margaret of Austria, Duchess of Savoy</span><span class="tp">1480–1530</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/charles-de-foucauld"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/charles-de-foucauld.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Charles de Foucauld</span><span class="tp">1858–1916</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/damrong-rajanubhab"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/damrong-rajanubhab.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Damrong Rajanubhab</span><span class="tp">1862–1943</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/david-ben-gurion"><span class="ph ph-person" aria-hidden="true"></span><span><span class="nm">David Ben-Gurion</span><span class="tp">1886–1973</span></span></a></li></ul></section>
<p class="day-ppl-note">Dates as the sources give them: in the Julian calendar before 1582, and in some countries for longer (Britain until 1752, Russia until 1918). Only people whose day of birth or death the records agree on are listed.</p>
